  So now new medical data states that the bullet entered Charlie's neck at
  C2, obliterated C3, C4, C5, C6, C7 and then lodged in T1. Also, Charlie
  was leaning slightly forward when he was struck by the round, slightly to
  the left of his Adam's Apple. So with that gradual 10° downward angle, it
  should've entered around C7 or T1. With the height of the roof and range
  that Robinson was at, it's mathematically impossible for the bullet to
  enter at C2. C2 is nowhere close the wound in his neck. Or perhaps the
  bullet hit T1 bounced un to CO and then back down to T1
  Atithis
